      "writtenOn": "2016-02-26T13:22:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So my one bit of unease about this, is that it feels odd that if I have a token for Project A, with roles X, Y in it, that as I run down the hierarchy, I might call policy on a subproject with MORE roles that I had in the original token (i.e. if I also had role Z on subproject B, then I\u0027d call policy with roles X, Y and Z). This feels wrong.\n\nHow about saying that the roles you pass to policy will always be a subset of the ones in the initial token (where subset \u003d the same or less roles)?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 277,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 288,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "c21399c742a221ae095106ff24037bbbfd00679c",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
